In article <18778@bellcore.bellcore.com> raj@dduck.UUCP (Randy Jackson) writes:
>
>2) When exiting a room all objects which are in the room remain
>   visable to you until they are moved (or rot in the case of corpses).
>   You then see the object dissappear even though you are in a different
>   room.

I've always thought of this as being what I remembered about what was in the
room.  Things should not disappear when they are moved or used by monsters
but when you re-enter the room, the room should be redrawn so that you see
what the room actually looks like "now".  If you want to get real
sophisticated you might change the code so that your "memory" fades after a
certain amount of time.  The amount of time could be based on your
intellegence and/or wisdom.

But this seems like a somewhat minor issues.  Although it does often tip me
off to the presence of other monsters in certain rooms.  But telepathy and
a blind fold will do the same thing.
